From: TheMoon <execorvo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build.sh: default to --lto=thin, not Kconfig's implicit default

A --lto=full build caused a real on-device bootloop (freeze at the
bootloader logo, then a shutdown) on our MT6768 device. Most likely
cause: CONFIG_CFI_CLANG=y combined with Full LTO's more aggressive
whole-program optimization exposed an indirect-call type mismatch in
untested MTK vendor driver code -- CFI panics deterministically and
very early in boot on that kind of mismatch. Reverting to --lto=thin
fixed it; if your kernel also has CFI enabled, don't assume Full LTO
is safe on vendor driver code that's never been built with it before.

Also (unrelated, just convenience) wires up an optional Neutron Clang
toolchain via --user_clang_toolchain, gated behind USE_NEUTRON_CLANG
and left disabled by default -- it broke Bazel's hermetic host tools
for us (missing libc++ headers/runtime, sysroot mismatches). Feel free
to drop that hunk if you don't want Neutron Clang support at all.

Applies to: kernel_device_modules-6.6/build.sh
---
diff --git a/build.sh b/build.sh
index 4df14394aca4..cd6f6b2477aa 100755
--- a/build.sh
+++ b/build.sh
@@ -26,10 +26,11 @@ KLEAF_ARGS=("${DEBUG_ARGS} ${SANDBOX_ARGS} \
 	--experimental_writable_outputs \
 	--noenable_bzlmod \
 	--config=stamp \
+	--lto=thin \
 	--//build/bazel_mgk_rules:kernel_version=${KERNEL_VERSION_NUM}")

 NEUTRON_CLANG_DIR="${ROOT_DIR}/prebuilts/neutron-clang"
-if [ "${USE_NEUTRON_CLANG:-1}" != "0" ] && [ -x "${NEUTRON_CLANG_DIR}/bin/clang" ]; then
+if [ "${USE_NEUTRON_CLANG:-0}" != "0" ] && [ -x "${NEUTRON_CLANG_DIR}/bin/clang" ]; then
   KLEAF_ARGS="${KLEAF_ARGS} --user_clang_toolchain=${NEUTRON_CLANG_DIR}"
 fi

